<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106119" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑάδες</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ων</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, αἱ</span> (sg. in collect. sense, <i><span class="en">
			Ptol.
			<u>Tetr.</u>
			94
		</span></i>, <u>Gloss.</u>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the Hyades,</i> a group of stars in the head of the Bull,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.486
			</span></i>; their morning setting (in November) was a rainy season,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				615
			</span></i>; hence commonly derived fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕω,</span> Lat. <i>Pluviae,</i> Verg.<i><span class="en">
				<u>A.</u>
				1.744
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.516
			</span></i>, Ov.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fast.</u>
				5.166
			</span></i>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὕης</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>; but in Lat. usu. called <i>suculae, piglings,</i> as if
			fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὗς, ὑός,</span> Tiroap.<i><span class="en">
				Gell.
				13.9.4
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ</span> is short in 
				Ep.
			, though <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span> in
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				1156
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				468
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> five
			Nymphs named by <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				180
			</span></i>; later of the Nymphs who reared Dionysus, <i><span class="en">
				Pherecyd.
				90
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς βάκχας Ὑάδας ἔλεγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔναστρος.</span>
			</div>
